Spec: Shared kernel

Purpose:
  Cross-cutting pieces used by every feature package: the single SQLite connection, the shared page shell and the
  Europe/Helsinki date policy. It holds no domain rules and no routes.

Owns:
  ./db.py
  ./ids.py
  ./layout.py
  ./dates.py
  ./static/app.css
  ./static/favicon.svg

References:
  ../architecture.sdd
  /Dockerfile

Must:
  ./db.py exposes @create_database, which opens a `fastlite` `Database` at `/data/app.db` (or a caller-given
  path), creating the parent directory when it does not exist. main.py calls it once and passes the single
  connection into every feature's repository_sqlite.py constructor, per ../architecture.sdd.
  ./ids.py exposes @parse_id, which turns a route path or query value into the integer id the services expect,
  returning `None` for an empty or non-numeric value so a route can treat it as absent; routes.py parse ids
  with it instead of passing raw strings to services.py.
  ./layout.py renders the shared page shell: header, a `<link>` to the hand-written stylesheet and the HTMX
  script tag, used by every feature's view.py.
  ./layout.py also emits one inline script for the whole page that keeps a hover tooltip inside the visible area:
    an element marked `data-tip` is the tooltip's anchor, its `data-tip-body` child is the tooltip, and the tooltip
    is kept inside the nearest `data-tip-area` ancestor, or the viewport when there is none. On hover the script
    centres the tooltip on its anchor, opens it below the anchor when there is no room above, and clamps it to the
    area's edges, so a tooltip never leaves the viewport or slides under the header. The reveal stays in CSS, so an
    anchor still shows its tooltip when the script is unavailable.
  ./static/app.css is the site's whole stylesheet: hand-written vanilla CSS with semantic class names, committed
  to the repository; it is never generated, minified or processed, per /aikana.sdd's Forbids.
  `main.py` serves ./static/app.css at `/static/app.css` via `app.static_route`, using `layout.STATIC_DIR` so the
    path resolves regardless of the process's working directory.
  ./static/favicon.svg is the site's icon: `main.py` serves it at `/static/favicon.svg` and ./layout.py links it as
    `rel="icon"` with type `image/svg+xml`, since `app.static_route` serves a single extension per call and the
    stylesheet's `.css` route does not cover it.
  ./layout.py's header is the same top bar on every view: on the left the `Aikana` brand and a horizontal nav
  linking the Semester view (`/`), the Courses view (`/courses`) and the Realization view (`/realizations`) in that
  order, highlighting whichever one the calling route registers as active; on the right a persistent Semester
  selector, an admin-only `+ New Semester` link (rendered whenever the calling route passes `is_admin`) and the
  login/logout link. It takes the active link name, the Semester selector's `(id, label)` options and selected id
  and plain flags and rendered controls as arguments, so it still needs no feature imports. A view's own selector
  control (for example ../realizations/realizations.sdd's CourseRealization dropdown) lives in that view, not in
  the shared header.
  The header renders the persistent Semester selector whenever the calling route passes at least one option, on
  every tab. Changing it re-renders the current tab through the `semester_id` query parameter without a full page
  reload, and the nav links carry the selected `semester_id`, so the selection persists across tabs.
  ./layout.py exposes @dropdown as the shared select renderer: name, `(id, label)` options, selected id, the
    `hx_get` path to re-render, and an optional `hx_include`; the shell's Semester selector and a feature view.py's
    own selector use it, so all selects behave consistently.
  ./layout.py exposes @day_calendar as the shared Monday-first month calendar: a weekday header running `Mon` to
    `Sun`, the selected date's month as whole Monday-to-Sunday weeks, and one `day` radio input per day cell with
    `selected` checked, so the grid is the form's own field and picking a day needs no script. The browser's own date
    picker orders its weeks by the browser's locale, which starts on Sunday in many of them and cannot be re-ordered
    from the page, so a feature that must show a Finnish week renders this grid instead of an `<input type="date">`.
  ./layout.py's header also takes an already-rendered login/logout link as a plain argument, per
  ../auth/auth.sdd, so it still needs no import of ../auth/auth.sdd's services.py or routes.py.
  The header's groups wrap onto further lines instead of squeezing on a narrow viewport, and the title and each nav
  label stay on one line rather than breaking mid-label, so the shared shell stays readable on a phone-sized screen
  without changing its desktop layout.
  ./dates.py is the single source of the date policy in ../aikana.sdd: @today returns the current date in
    `Europe/Helsinki` regardless of the host's time zone, @format_date renders a calendar date in the European
    `d.m.yyyy` form, and @month_grid returns the month containing a date as Monday-first weeks of seven days padded
    with `None` before its first and after its last day, so a rendered week or month always starts on its Monday.

Must not:
  ./db.py and ./layout.py must not import any feature package's domain.py, ports.py, services.py,
  repository_sqlite.py, view.py or routes.py.

Tasks:
  [x] Implement ./layout.py with the shared page shell (header plus the Tailwind Play CDN and HTMX headers) for the
    first hardcoded semester-view pass
  [x] Extend ./layout.py's header with the horizontal top-bar nav between the Semester and Realization views and a
    slot for each view's own selector dropdown
  [x] Implement ./db.py: the shared `fastlite` `Database` connection at `/data/app.db`, now that real persistence
    begins
  [x] Replace the lazy module-level connection in ./db.py with the @create_database factory so main.py builds the
    single `Database` and injects it into each repository, per ../architecture.sdd
  [x] Replace the Tailwind Play CDN script (cdn.tailwindcss.com is unsupported for production) with a Tailwind CLI
    build: add ./static/input.css, compile ./static/app.css with the standalone CLI in the `css` stage of
    /Dockerfile, serve it from `main.py` via `app.static_route`, and update ./layout.py to link it instead of
    injecting the CDN `<script>`
  [x] Emit the page-wide tooltip positioning script from ./layout.py's `extra_headers`, so any view.py's hover
    tooltip can be marked as an anchor and kept inside its area
  [x] Add @month_grid to ./dates.py and @day_calendar to ./layout.py, so every rendered week and month starts on its
    Monday and a form can pick a day without a browser date picker
  [x] Let ./layout.py's header wrap its groups onto further lines and keep the title and nav labels unwrapped, so the
    shared shell stays readable on a phone-sized screen
  [x] Add ./static/favicon.svg and link it from ./layout.py, served by a second `app.static_route` in `main.py`
  [x] Replace the Tailwind CLI build with the hand-written vanilla ./static/app.css: committed source with semantic
    class names, no `css` stage in /Dockerfile and no input.css; ./layout.py links it unchanged at `/static/app.css`
